    "Nothing is offered, whatever the entry says, when: the picked Point is the picked circle's or arc's centre; the circle's or arc's centre is an end of the picked line; two circles or arcs share one centre Point.",
    "Two Points that lie on two different parallel lines (an end or a midpoint of each) are read as those two lines: the line+line lines_parallel entry, not point+point.",
    "Picking: at most two picks; a third pick restarts the selection unless all three are Points; picking a picked entity again removes it.",
    "A spline, a text, a lone Point, and an ellipse or elliptical arc with anything else have no options."
